Lithic

The interface uses Lithic, Ryoku's design language and Go UI library. Lithic is
part of the Ryoku repository under GPL-3.0-only. The `ryotunes` client links
Lithic, so that binary is distributed under GPLv3 only.

Project history and retained work

Ryotunes 2.x is an original Ryoku Go codebase. It does not compile or ship the
1.x Rust, QML, Svelte or JavaScript source. It keeps the Ryotunes app icon and
some Linux package metadata from 1.x, and it preserves the data paths and wire
contract so existing libraries, settings and sessions still work.

Ryotunes 1.x began as a modified GPL-3.0-or-later work based on LiMusic by
SimoHypers and contributors:

  https://github.com/SimoHypers/limusic

The YouTube client profile table in internal/provider/youtube/clients.go was
carried from the GPL-3.0 1.x and LiMusic table. Those values keep the same
GPL-3.0-compatible terms and LiMusic credit.

The lyric romanization logic in internal/lyrics/romanize is ported from
PeekMusic at commit 83217188a, itself a fork of Metrolist. PeekMusic is
GPL-3.0, and this port remains under GPL-3.0-compatible terms:

  https://github.com/PeekMusic/PeekMusic
  https://github.com/MetrolistGroup/Metrolist

Third-party components

The four Go binaries use the modules listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES. Only the
`ryotunesd` daemon links go-librespot, which is GPL-3.0-only, so that binary is
distributed under GPLv3 only. The Space Grotesk and Space Mono fonts are
OFL-1.1. Material Design icons are Apache-2.0.

The pinned xlab/vorbis-go revision predates that repository's LICENSE file. The
copyright holder now publishes vorbis-go under MIT. A verbatim copy of that
current grant is kept in release/notices/xlab-vorbis-go.LICENSE and included in
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.

Ryotunes also uses system components without bundling them into its Go
binaries. It loads libmpv, runs yt-dlp and FFmpeg for stream and download work,
and can run cava and PipeWire's pw-record and pw-dump for visualizers. Their
licenses come with their system packages: mpv is GPL-2.0-or-later by default or
LGPL-2.1-or-later when built in LGPL mode, yt-dlp is Unlicense, cava and
PipeWire are MIT, and FFmpeg is LGPL-2.1-or-later or GPL depending on its build.
